s", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 56, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[86, 86]], "assertion": "continuous covariates (height, weight, games) were standardized to mean 0, SD 1", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["height", "weight", "games played"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 57, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[87, 88]], "assertion": "categorical covariates were dummy-coded with one reference category", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["categorical covariates"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 58, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[89, 89]], "note": "Standard Error/Clustering Choice subheading"}, {"id": 59, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[90, 92]], "assertion": "player-level clustering (a conservative approach) was chosen because it accounts for within-player correlation and is more appropriate given skin tone is a player-level characteristic", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["clustering", "standard errors"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 60, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[93, 94]], "assertion": "player-level clustering produces larger standard errors than referee-level clustering", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["standard errors", "clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 61, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[95, 96]], "assertion": "referee-level clustering was also reported as a sensitivity check", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["clustering", "sensitivity analysis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 62, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[97, 98]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 63, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[99, 100]], "note": "Section 4 heading"}, {"id": 64, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[101, 102]], "assertion": "based on the primary player-clustered estimand, the hypothesis is NOT SUPPORTED at α=0.05", "polarity": "found", "target